{
  "$comment": "SDK v1 capability catalog (user spec 2026-09-30, sdk/API.md). 'core' calls need no permission (plugin info, lifecycle, logger, config, utils, locale, resources, rate limits). Every other call needs its permission switched on in the SDK policies (admin > SDK Policies, table sdk_policies; default: risk low = on, otherwise off) and declared in the plugin manifest. Plugins never get a database handle, the bot token, environment variables or direct network access; every call goes through the SDK manager in the bot. 'implemented' lists the calls the manager answers today; the others answer sdk.call.not_available. Texts: dashboard lang keys sdk.perm.<key> and sdk.perm.<key>_hint. Every permission has a main \"group\" (the SDK policies page shows the groups alphabetically, each one opens to its permissions). \"replaced\" maps old coarse keys to the finer ones: a manifest that names an old key is read as if it named the new keys. Discord events: a plugin needs the discord.events.* permission whose \"events\" list holds the event. Module permissions: modules.<module>.<area>; \"scope\": \"module\" entries (modules.<key>.read) share the module.* calls of modules.read, which allows every module, while modules.<key>.read allows that one module only.",
